In article <1dsld6INNdkh@escargot.xx.rmit.OZ.AU>, s892341@minyos.xx.rmit.oz.au (Matt=Goodall) writes:
|> 
|> 	A look command similiar to Moria would be nice, also when a wand
|> is out of charges and you haven't identified it yet having the computer
|> declare it (empty) would also save some of my characters. Bags of holding
|> and other containers should be changed so that you can see all the items
|> in them and choose what to take out by class of object.
|> 
What does the Moria look command do? There are look (at the current square)
and specify object commands to see all discovered areas. 
One of the main qualities of wands is that you do not know how many charges
they have unless you identify them, sow how would you know an empty wand unless
you zap it and nothing happens?
I agree that there could be a better way of accessing bags (and chests) than
simply going through the whole list of items.

